2026-09-28: bounded single-device controls PASS; K04 remains OPEN.

This is a diagnostic reduction, not unchanged upstream stress_04 acceptance.
The reference-built C program exercises one owned device at a time on the
retained matching GCC/EvoCC Images. It never signals a host process or modifies
the backing runtime disks. Modes match the installed upstream server:
  cold null: -z --no_ublk_fixed_fd; --auto_zc; --nthreads 8 --per_io_tasks;
             -z --auto_zc --auto_zc_fallback (4 cases)
  warm loop: first three modes, independent 64 MiB backing file (3 cases)

Cold controls stop the new daemon before submission. Warm controls require
at least 64 new completed requests, run buffered I/O, stop that daemon and
explicitly request fdatasync. Both require a positive outstanding-request
count before killing the daemon. The small loop working set can fit in cache;
without explicit writeback a zero request count is not a kernel failure.
Each client has an 8-second completion bound; device deletion also has an
8-second bound. Expected client I/O error exit 4 is distinguished from missing
executables/setup errors. The original selftest budget is not changed.

